WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.000
Welcome back to The David Pakman Show, I am
Jesse Delmore, out of work stunt double for

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.410
Jim Gaffigan Show.

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:11.539
Yesterday, something happened that we've been
waiting for for many years, and that is an

00:00:11.539 --> 00:00:12.919
infrastructure bill to pass.

00:00:12.919 --> 00:00:17.840
During the Trump administration, it seemed
like infrastructure week was every week in

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:19.760
perpetuity.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.700
Materialize into nothing.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:29.110
And we passed less than we wanted, less than
we need, certainly less than we deserve, but

00:00:29.110 --> 00:00:31.009
better than nothing.

00:00:31.009 --> 00:00:34.970
Reading from this New York Times article entitled
Senate Passes One Trillion Dollar Infrastructure

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:37.980
Bill and even Biden a bipartisan win.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:42.860
The approval came after months of negotiations
and despite deficit concerns, reflecting an

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:47.899
appetite in both parties for a long awaited
spending package.

00:00:47.899 --> 00:00:55.750
So the vote ended up being 69 to 30, which
is telling that they were able to get nearly

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:58.840
20 Republicans on board.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:04.119
Even Mitch McConnell, in fact, the Senate
gave overwhelming bipartisan approval on Tuesday

00:01:04.119 --> 00:01:09.299
to a one trillion dollar infrastructure bill
to rebuild the nation's deteriorating roads

00:01:09.299 --> 00:01:14.030
and bridges and fund new climate resilience
and broadband initiatives, delivering a key

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:16.750
component of President Biden's agenda.

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:21.570
The vote, 69 to 30, was uncommonly bipartisan.

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:27.119
The yes votes included Senator Mitch McConnell
of Kentucky, the Republican leader, and 18

00:01:27.119 --> 00:01:33.290
others from his party who shrugged off increasingly
shrill efforts by former President Donald

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:36.240
J. Trump to derail.

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:44.740
It is the last part of that sentence because
that was indeed the M.O. has been the M.O.

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:47.799
of Trump and the Republicans for a long time.

00:01:47.799 --> 00:01:51.520
I am still weary of what is happening.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:54.810
Wari, excuse me of what's happening here.

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:55.930
What is to take place?

00:01:55.930 --> 00:02:04.250
What's the what Machiavellian motivations
do they have for overwhelmingly or for Republicans?

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:07.539
It's overwhelming support of this bill.

00:02:07.539 --> 00:02:11.960
The historic investment in infrastructure
is what I believe you, the American people

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:17.890
want what you've been asking for for a long,
long time, Mr. Biden said from the White House

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:22.220
as he thanked Republicans for showing a lot
of courage.

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:29.360
Because in today's day and age, it is courage
to support an infrastructure bill that is

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:37.110
desperately needed as our bridges and our
tunnels and our roadways and our infrastructure

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:39.100
is literally crumbling.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:45.140
Mr McConnell, who publicly declared that his
priority was stopping the Biden agenda, said

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:50.290
in a statement that, quote, I was proud to
support today's historic bipartisan infrastructure

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:56.590
deal and prove that both sides of the political
aisle can still come together around common

00:02:56.590 --> 00:02:58.920
sense solutions.

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:06.060
If it were coming from anybody other than
Mitch McConnell, I might believe it.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:11.480
The measure faces a potentially rocky and
time consuming path in the House, where Speaker

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:16.730
Nancy Pelosi and a majority of the nearly
100 member progressive caucus had said they

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:22.690
will not vote on it unless the Senate passes
a separate, even more ambitious three point

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:27.560
five trillion dollar social policy bill this
fall that could put the infrastructure bill

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:30.480
on hold for weeks, if not months.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:35.650
And the the method by which they intend to
press the Senate to pass that three point

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:41.960
five trillion dollar appropriation is through
reconciliation where they won't need.

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:43.950
They could bypass the filibuster.

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:48.490
They could bypass Republican obstructionism.

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:55.350
Here is a little larger context, a little
longer context of what Joe Biden said in his

00:03:55.350 --> 00:03:56.350
speech.

00:03:56.350 --> 00:04:03.320
Speaker 3: First of all, I want to thank a
group of senators, Democrats and Republicans,

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:08.010
for doing what they told me they would do.

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:13.850
The death of this legislation was mildly premature,
as reported.

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:19.090
They said they're willing to work in a bipartisan
manner and I want to thank them for keeping

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:20.090
their word.

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:22.040
That's just what they did.

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:28.510
After years and years of infrastructure week,
we're in the cusp of an infrastructure decade

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:30.930
that I truly believe will transform America.

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:36.910
Speaker 1: So it was a good day for the country,
certainly a good day from an agenda agenda

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:39.560
standpoint for President Biden.

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:41.730
There was another side, though.

00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:47.100
That is the side of Mike Lee, Republican from
Utah.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:50.870
He is Ted Cruz without a beard, not quite
as salacious.

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:57.660
He's a little bit more milquetoast, but certainly
an obstructionist, certainly someone who is

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:02.290
whose agenda is marked by his ability to not
vote for things.

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:06.670
That's his that's his his pride and glory.

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:09.650
Is his ability to not vote?

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:10.650
Here's Mike Lee.

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:12.680
Speaker 5: People are still digesting it.

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:15.760
Members of the Senate are still digesting
it.

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:24.180
Look, we're in a period of great inflation
brought on by a period of almost unfettered,

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:26.950
unrestrained federal spending.

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:31.830
It bears no connection, it seems, to the laws
of mathematics or to the amount of money that

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:33.330
were brought in.

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:37.370
This bill would spend a staggering one point
two trillion dollars.

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:42.210
It would be yet another inflation bomb in
an economy that's already been carpet bombed

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:44.170
by other inflation bombs.

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:49.571
If I grasp the fact that it's difficult to
put together a bipartisan package, I have

00:05:49.571 --> 00:05:53.460
nothing but respect for each of our colleagues
who were part of this effort.

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:57.670
I also am willing to acknowledge that the
bill does a lot of good things and would help

00:05:57.670 --> 00:05:58.970
a lot of deserving beneficiaries.

00:05:58.970 --> 00:06:03.170
There are a lot of people who would benefit
in a lot of ways from it, but there is a huge

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:04.170
problem with it.

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:08.290
It is not paid for the reason that we know
that that's a problem, that it's not paid

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:09.290
for.

00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:14.230
Is that the one consistent refrain that you
hear from its sponsors, other than the fact

00:06:14.230 --> 00:06:18.780
that it's bipartisan, which which we know
and which we respect is the fact that it's

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:20.160
paid for.

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:22.900
They'll say over and over again that this
bill is paid for.

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:26.580
But when you look at the pays, the pay fors,
they don't add up.

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:31.830
When you have papers that don't actually pay,
you're just going to add to the debt and deficit

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:34.550
and this isn't a good time to be doing that.

00:06:34.550 --> 00:06:38.140
Speaker 1: It never ceases to amaze me and
never will cease to amaze me.

00:06:38.140 --> 00:06:41.300
These Republicans who.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:46.160
Who pride themselves now on on how is this
going to be paid for?

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:48.620
How are we ever going to pay for those?

00:06:48.620 --> 00:06:51.620
We're saddling our children with debt.

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:58.910
As though this is a household and debt means
the same thing as you owning a car and having

00:06:58.910 --> 00:07:01.960
credit card debt, it is not the same thing.

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:08.300
But to where was Mike Lee during the Donald
Trump administration that was running up one

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:13.990
and one and a half trillion dollar deficits
while things were good economically in the

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:14.990
country?

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:19.500
Where were you, Mike Lee?

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:21.860
Where were you?

00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:28.300
It just rings hollow now listen, I would I
would be lying if I didn't say that I'm a

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:34.790
little nervous about the aggressiveness of
the progressives in Congress, the squad who

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:39.010
I am almost universally a fan of.

00:07:39.010 --> 00:07:46.540
But if if they push this too far and we get
nothing and they give the Republicans an excuse.

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:53.800
To back out and not vote for or for whatever
conference agreement they come to on a bill,

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:56.680
then we've lost, then we get nothing.

00:07:56.680 --> 00:08:00.410
We don't even get the one or one point two
trillion, we get zero.

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:07.360
And we're back to square one with the infrastructure
week, week after week.

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:09.110
Kind of a situation.

00:08:09.110 --> 00:09:10.510
Not good.

